  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nHere is an example using Qwik framework:\r\n\r\n1. On load change the url to append a new query param\r\n2. Push state\r\n3. Click go back - expected to not go back since I pushed a new state, but it does go back\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport { component$, useVisibleTask$ } from '@builder.io/qwik'\r\n\r\nexport default component$(() => {\r\n    useVisibleTask$(() => {\r\n        window.history.replaceState({ modal: false }, '', `http://localhost:5173/testing?modal=true`)\r\n\r\n        window.addEventListener('popstate', () => {\r\n            alert(JSON.stringify(window.history.state))\r\n        })\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    return (\r\n        <>\r\n            <button\r\n                onClick$={() => {\r\n                    window.history.pushState({ modal: true }, '')\r\n                }}\r\n            >\r\n                Push State\r\n            </button>\r\n        </>\r\n    )\r\n})\r\n\r\n```",
